        &lt;source_vulnerability_explanation&gt;&lt;![CDATA[We tracked the following data from &amp;#34;path&amp;#34; Parameter:&lt;br /&gt;GET /getphoto?path&amp;#61;test_cat.jpg&lt;br /&gt;...which was accessed within the following code:&lt;br /&gt;Program.&amp;lt;&amp;gt;c__DisplayClass0_0.&amp;lt;$&amp;gt;b__2(), line 99&lt;br /&gt;...and ended up being used as part of the path in the following file being opened:&lt;br /&gt;/app/uploads/test_cat.jpg]]&gt;&lt;/source_vulnerability_explanation&gt;
        &lt;source_vulnerability_summary&gt;&lt;![CDATA[Because there is untrusted data being used as part of the file path, it may be possible for an attacker to read sensitive data or write, update, or delete arbitrary files on the container&amp;#39;s file system. The ability to write arbitrary files to the file system is also called Unrestricted or Arbitrary File Uploads.]]&gt;&lt;/source_vulnerability_summary&gt;
